session 24: scripts/pool.py, the pooled estimates over both draws, committed before the second draw is embedded

Step 1 recomputes, for each draw alone, every row it pools from the per-query files the pod pushes and compares each line with the line s19.py or budget.py printed, character for character; one difference stops it before any pooled number. On S19 all fourteen lines are reproduced (H19a, H19b, H19c, the no-code and all-of-P1/P2 rows, cs - d, H19d, H21a, H21b, H21c). Step 2 pools: queries of both draws in a test's cell, owner-weighted mean, an owner in both draws counted once, 10,000 owner resamples, seeds 24101 and up. Checked on a copy of S19 posing as the second draw: every pooled point and owner count equals the single draw's.

data/notok_code_s19_e1.txt: the two code files of S19 that E1 did not embed (from the cache index on the pod), so that a no-code folder is the one s19.py counted.

